From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: keep the priority of an 802.3 frame for the slow path

ieee80211_8023_xmit() classifies a frame with ieee80211_select_queue()
before it checks the aggregation session of its TID. While that session
is not operational, it passes the frame to
__ieee80211_subif_start_xmit(), which classifies it again. The first
classification replaced a priority of 256 to 263 by the UP it names, so
the second one takes the UP from the DSCP. The frames of a new flow that
are sent during the ADDBA exchange thus go out with another TID than the
frames after it.

Give the slow path the priority that the frame had on entry, so that
both paths classify it the same way.

Fixes: 96ae9cd02c0f ("mac80211: check and refresh aggregation session in encap offload tx")
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>

--- a/net/mac80211/tx.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/tx.c
@@ -4910,6 +4910,7 @@ static void ieee80211_8023_xmit(struct i
 	struct tid_ampdu_tx *tid_tx = NULL;
 	struct sk_buff *seg, *next;
 	unsigned int skbs = 0, len = 0;
+	u32 priority = skb->priority;
 	u32 ctrl_flags = 0;
 	u16 queue;
 	u8 tid;
@@ -4933,7 +4934,11 @@ static void ieee80211_8023_xmit(struct i
 		tid_tx = rcu_dereference(sta->ampdu_mlme.tid_tx[tid]);
 	if (tid_tx) {
 		if (!test_bit(HT_AGG_STATE_OPERATIONAL, &tid_tx->state)) {
-			/* fall back to non-offload slow path */
+			/*
+			 * fall back to non-offload slow path, which classifies
+			 * the frame again
+			 */
+			skb->priority = priority;
 			__ieee80211_subif_start_xmit(skb, dev, 0,
 						     IEEE80211_TX_CTRL_MLO_LINK_UNSPEC,
 						     NULL);
